# Exporter authoring

Exporters in `packages/exporters-*` generate **standalone framework-native source** from Export IR — they never parse canvas JSON.

## Contract

Implement `ExporterPlugin` (`packages/core/src/lib/export/exporter-plugin.ts`):

- `generate(ir, options) => GeneratedFile[]`
- Declare `targetKind`: `'ui' | 'server' | 'database'`
- Register in server export dispatch — no special cases in `export.service.ts`

## IR-only input

- Read `ExportIR`, `IRComponent`, `IRLayout`, `IRDataSource` — not `ComponentNode`
- If a field is missing from IR, extend `build-export-ir.ts` — do not read composite files in exporter

## Standalone-first

Default export options must emit **complete source** with **no required `@rosettadash/*` import** in generated app code (`02-standalone-first-export.mdc`).

- Package mode (`exportMode: 'package'`) is opt-in only
- Third-party deps (three, ffmpeg) documented in `README.export.md` — not RosettaDash runtime deps

## New palette types

Adding a `ComponentDefinition` requires **every UI exporter** update (or export matrix tests fail):

1. React exporter minimum
2. Angular, Vue, Svelte, web-components when touching matrix
3. Stable generated file paths — no random suffixes
4. UTF-8 text; binary assets out of scope unless explicitly supported

## Secrets and env

- Never embed secret values — env var placeholders + `.env.example` only
- Generated config accessors read from env at runtime

## Styling in exports

- Prefer converging new work on `rd-*` / `--rd-*` in generated components
- Stack profiles (Tailwind, MUI, plain CSS) follow wizard choice (`docs/41-stack-styling-guides.md`)

## Server stub pattern

Role header stub: `x-rosettadash-role` for generated server auth — consistent across server exporters.

## Tests

- Guard wrong `ir.targets.ui`
- Fixture dashboard in matrix fixtures
- Binding-heavy component coverage
- Assert standalone default has no `@rosettadash/` imports

